            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi!\r\n\r\nI'd assume you are using `clangd`. It has `--limit-results` option for \"Limit the number of results returned by clangd. 0 means no limit (default=100).\" So if you want a bigger number, supply a different value during LSP server initialization. For example, if done directly (not with 'nvim-lspconfig'): `vim.lsp.start({ name = 'clangd', cmd = { 'clangd', '--limit-results=1000' }, root_dir = vim.fn.getcwd()})`",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'd assume you are using <code class=\"notranslate\">clangd</code>. It has <code class=\"notranslate\">--limit-results</code> option for \"Limit the number of results returned by clangd. 0 means no limit (default=100).\" So if you want a bigger number, supply a different value during LSP server initialization. For example, if done directly (not with 'nvim-lspconfig'): <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.lsp.start({ name = 'clangd', cmd = { 'clangd', '--limit-results=1000' }, root_dir = vim.fn.getcwd()})</code></p>",
            "bodyText": "Hi!\nI'd assume you are using clangd. It has --limit-results option for \"Limit the number of results returned by clangd. 0 means no limit (default=100).\" So if you want a bigger number, supply a different value during LSP server initialization. For example, if done directly (not with 'nvim-lspconfig'): vim.lsp.start({ name = 'clangd', cmd = { 'clangd', '--limit-results=1000' }, root_dir = vim.fn.getcwd()})",
